<!DOCTYPE template>
<!--
  Description:
    Per-deck timecode signal status. Read-only.

    This is the piece no existing Mixxx skin provides. Every community
    small-screen skin is a controller companion built for jog wheels and pads,
    so none surfaces vinyl control state. On a DVS appliance this is the only
    troubleshooting surface for the timecode path: nothing on the mixer or the
    turntables reports whether Mixxx is actually reading the control signal.

    Values come from src/vinylcontrol/defs_vinylcontrol.h:
      0 VINYL_STATUS_DISABLED   vinyl control is off for this deck
      1 VINYL_STATUS_OK         timecode locked and tracking
      2 VINYL_STATUS_WARNING    signal degraded - dirty stylus, low level, worn record
      3 VINYL_STATUS_ERROR      no usable timecode

    Rendered as text on a block rather than a pixmap, so it needs no image
    asset and recolours with the palette like everything else.

    displayValue only: there is no ButtonState connection, so the widget has no
    control to write to and a stray touch does nothing.

  Variables:
    ChanNum: deck number, 1 or 2
-->
<Template>
  <PushButton>
    <ObjectName>DvsStatusLight</ObjectName>
    <Tooltip>Timecode signal status for this deck.

off  - vinyl control disabled
ok   - timecode locked and tracking
warn - signal degraded (stylus, level, worn record)
err  - no usable timecode</Tooltip>
    <Size>116f,38f</Size>
    <NumberStates>4</NumberStates>
    <State>
      <Number>0</Number>
      <Text>tc off</Text>
    </State>
    <State>
      <Number>1</Number>
      <Text>tc ok</Text>
    </State>
    <State>
      <Number>2</Number>
      <Text>tc warn</Text>
    </State>
    <State>
      <Number>3</Number>
      <Text>tc err</Text>
    </State>
    <Connection>
      <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="ChanNum"/>],vinylcontrol_status</ConfigKey>
      <BindProperty>displayValue</BindProperty>
    </Connection>
  </PushButton>
</Template>
